      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3\n0 3 3\n0 2 2\n2\n2 3\n0 1",
        "output": "1\n3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: An optimal good array is X=[0,3,2]X = [0, 3, 2]X=[0,3,2].\n\nFor i=1i = 1i=1: A1=X1=0A_1 = X_1 = 0A1​=X1​=0 and B1=X1B_1 = X_1B1​=X1​ &\\&& X2X_2X2​ &\\&& X3=0X_3 = 0X3​=0.\nFor i=2i = 2i=2: A2=X1A_2 = X_1A2​=X1​ ∣|∣ X2=3X_2 = 3X2​=3 and B2=X2B_2 = X_2B2​=X2​ &\\&& X3=2X_3 = 2X3​=2.\nFor i=3i = 3i=3: A3=X1A_3 = X_1A3​=X1​ ∣|∣ X2X_2X2​ ∣|∣ X3=3X_3 = 3X3​=3 and B3=X3=2B_3 = X_3 = 2B3​=X3​=2.\n\nThe XOR of all elements of XXX is 0⊕3⊕2=10\\oplus 3\\oplus 2 = 10⊕3⊕2=1. It can be proven that this is the maximum XOR value for any XXX.\nTest case 222: An optimal good array is X=[2,1]X = [2, 1]X=[2,1].\n\nFor i=1i = 1i=1: A1=X1=2A_1 = X_1 = 2A1​=X1​=2 and B1=X1B_1 = X_1B1​=X1​ &\\&& X2=0X_2 = 0X2​=0.\nFor i=2i = 2i=2: A2=X1A_2 = X_1A2​=X1​ ∣|∣ X2=3X_2 = 3X2​=3 and B2=X2=1B_2 = X_2 = 1B2​=X2​=1.\n\nThe XOR of all elements of XXX is 2⊕1=32\\oplus 1 = 32⊕1=3. It can be proven that this is the maximum XOR value for any XXX."
      }
